we've all experienced the frustration  caused by congestive streets even though  sat-nav systems are supposed to alert  you to traffic jams Christian Bruggeman  says sometimes the systems are actually  part of the problem when there's a  detour around the traffic jam then every  vehicle with an intelligent navigation  system is alerted meaning every driver  that takes it ends up creating the next  traffic jam a new system is meant to  help prevent traffic congestion from  happening in the first place  Brueggemann has developed software that  gives each user an individual route as  soon as I get a suggested route that  route is simultaneously reserved for me  the software calculates how many cars  can travel a street at the same time if  one driver chooses a particular route  the system estimates when that car will  reach that street once the calculated  capacity is reached suggestions for  alternate routes are given to other  users his ending here on the left we see  the simulation with our cars and our  navigation system and on the right other  navigation systems you can clearly see  that with our reservation system  different routes are suggested to  different cars that optimally  distributes the traffic across the  infrastructure using the entire city  that means you reach your destination  much sooner on the right you can clearly  see that almost all vehicles are trying  to get through the main artery which  quickly leads to traffic congestion in  this area  it works well in the computer simulation  traffic flows up to 30% faster and even  twice as fast during rush hour but so  far not enough drivers use the app to  make it really effective so the idea is  for other manufacturers to integrate the  software into their sat-nav systems  you
 

